// Osysharp.Dns — the contract between code that writes DNS records and whichever company hosts the zone.
//
// One record shape (`DnsRecord`), a provider interface (`IDnsProvider`), an app setting naming the one to use
// (`app.Dns = new DnsSetup { … }`), and a provider that keeps its records in the app's own table (`LocalDnsProvider`)
// — for tests, for a local platform, and for reading what WOULD be written before a real provider is connected.
//
// ⚑ SHAPED LIKE Osysharp.Mail AND Osysharp.Sms, ON PURPOSE. A provider is an adapter package — `Osysharp.Dns.Cloudflare`
//   first — so the code that writes records changes provider by changing one setting, and nothing that writes changes
//   with it. Google Cloud DNS, Azure DNS and a self-hosted server are further adapters behind the same five verbs.
//
// ⚑ WHY THIS IS A PACKAGE AND NOT THE PLATFORM. Its first caller is the control plane (one record per placement, and
//   every zone's ACME DNS-01 challenge), and the control plane is an Osy#
//   app that already composes kits for exactly this kind of seam — its mail goes out through `Osysharp.Mail`. Nothing
//   here is called by platform C#: the zone agents never hold a DNS credential, they ask the control plane to publish
//   their challenge, so a kit can carry the contract and the platform needs no new surface.
//
// ⛔ ADD A TXT VALUE, NEVER OVERWRITE ONE. Two zones proving the same wildcard name publish two values at one
//   `_acme-challenge` name at the same time, and a provider whose "set" replaced the name's TXT records would make the
//   second zone's challenge erase the first's — each zone's renewal then fails at random, depending on who asked
//   last. The contract has no TXT setter at all: `AddTxtValue` and `RemoveTxtValue`, one value each.
package Osysharp.Dns {
  version "0.1.1";
  minPlatform "0.9.0";
  summary     "DNS records an app writes — one record shape, a pluggable provider, add-a-value TXT semantics, and a provider that keeps records in the app's own table.";
  model "model/*.osy";
  tests "tests";
}
